{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>You shall not pass through me.</b> That is, through the heart of my land — the route that is close to the land of Canaan; but they did pass through his land when they skirted Mount Seir, and this is what Moses mentions in the Mishneh Torah (Deuteronomy 2:29): ״כאשר עשו לי בני עשו היושבים בשעיר״ — as the children of Esau who dwell in Seir did for me — for Moses and Israel were asking Sihon to grant them permission to pass through his land just as the children of Esau had done, and there I shall write, with the help of El, may He be blessed." "<b>Lest I come out against you with the sword.</b> You pride yourselves on the voice you inherited from your father and say that you cry out and are answered, while I shall come out against you with what my father bequeathed me, as it is said (Genesis 27:39–40): ״ועל חרבך תחיה״ — and by your sword you shall live."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:19.917483301Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}